# `emit_abi` writes LF, and `tools/check_abi.js` byte-compares its output against the
# committed file. Under `core.autocrlf=true` git checks that file out as CRLF, so
# `npm run check:abi` fails on a clean freshly-checked-out tree -- and fails opaquely,
# reporting every one of its 221 lines as different while `diff` shows no visible
# change. Pinning the checkout to LF is what makes the generator and the gate agree.
#
# The two states are otherwise mutually exclusive: CRLF gives a clean `git status` and
# a failing `check:abi`, LF gives a passing `check:abi` and a file git reports as
# permanently modified. Neither is a tree anybody should have to work in.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the one generated file that is compared byte for byte, and not
# `* text=auto eol=lf`: that renormalises every file in the working tree at once, which
# is the same enormous unrelated diff AGENTS.md refuses `cargo fmt` for.
client/src/protocol/abi.generated.ts text eol=lf
